cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "A General Tool for Living Meta-Analysis"
abstract: >-
  A Shiny web application for interactive, reproducible living meta-analysis,
  supporting aggregated and multilevel effect-size models with frequentist
  (metafor) and Bayesian (bayesmeta, brms) estimation, meta-regression,
  correlated within-paper sampling errors, Bayes-factor robustness checks, and
  downloadable reproducible R scripts.
